side length one unit.\n\n![](images/87/870ab808de9f829e5967f4792119b4b596ad9de28ff714e1ce5c3b2b686338fb.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$." 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761409 1072 #uuid "07c2b492-d44f-5131-9a7b-db9206a3e7e1" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761409 1074 "Construct the known component $\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=\\frac{4}{3}\\,(3, 0)=(4, 0). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(4, -8).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/80/808f2835fcaf678e3cbde7898ac8af3893e9dc71ed879cff900aefc430393c74.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{4}{2}=2 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-8}{-4}=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=2\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{4}{3}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=2$." 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761410 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761410 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761410 1083 #uuid "093e41fc-a215-5606-a67a-9c58c29aad53" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761411 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761418 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761411 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761411 1071 "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/5f/5f32d62f2c3f23418be558580cc601f78c8a14154a77f805d58da57fcf0e49e7.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$." 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761411 1072 #uuid "0b0bfae0-92ed-5b58-bac6-9ee6206c2d11" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761411 1074 "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\\,(0, -3)=(0, -3). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{BC} &=(5, -10).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/5e/5e02968249ec36c4a1f3135bbffd984f2822275c0f2fb51b477a3ac4412b43e3.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(2, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-10}{-4}=\\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{BC}=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OB}+\\overrightarrow{BC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{b}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{5}{2}$." 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761412 1080 "3" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761412 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761412 1083 #uuid "0d035350-2aeb-5ee3-a2e6-1526c0b91813" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761413 1080 "1" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761413 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761413 1