rightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/5e/5e81fc8d41121ddfde878e3ba0aec7531eb29901282786e1915a408ae5e6af01.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}." 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761426 1072 #uuid "5b880935-6ff4-54af-834b-282c8fffc65e" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761426 1074 "Construct the known component $3\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &=3\\,(2, -2)=(6, -6). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PC} &=(-4, 0).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f5/f571ab2db29957aa8533bfb6fb602fb5c061fffb2d996ee60d6f8279e2fb19d9.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-2, 0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-4}{-2}=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{PC}=2\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC} \\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{b}+2\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=2$." 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761427 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761449 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761427 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761427 1071 "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/aa/aa82a832d995267377fc509465ad66fa2d1ae45020a1d7a6e1d59c634147e9b1.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$." 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761427 1072 #uuid "5bd1ee6d-05c9-56b6-8062-0b5bd06d6caa" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761427 1074 "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\\,(3, 0)=(3, 0). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{BC} &=(12, -12).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/3e/3e0501efbcbc85ddf1046ea01a03dea98ba5c9f8fa9d24c706b888b885ec71c6.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(4, -4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{12}{4}=3 \\\\\n\\text{Vertical scale} &=\\frac{-12}{-4}=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{BC}=3\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OB}+\\overrightarrow{BC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{b}+3\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=3$." 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761428 1080 "1" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761428 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761428 1083 #uuid "602968b2-2e20-5463-a891-c5361b16c4d8" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761429 1080 "2" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761429 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761429 1083 #uuid "6d481b42-e4bc-59fc-b6ce-4ec41bf84b6c" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761430 1080 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761430 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592186761430 1083 #uuid "6d891a84-a77f-5e89-8bee-0980d1efe5b2" 13194139547589 17592186576411 true] [17592